@*
    jQuery is loaded HERE rather than in a layout, deliberately.

    The two scripts below are jQuery plugins and do nothing without it — but no layout loaded jQuery
    at all, so every page including this partial threw "jQuery is not defined" and client-side
    validation never ran (audit T09 / issue #156). Nothing caught it because server-side validation
    still rejected bad input, so the pages behaved correctly, just less pleasantly: no inline errors
    until a round trip.

    Putting the dependency in the partial means it cannot go missing again by someone choosing the
    other layout. Neither _PublicLayout nor _AppLayout loads jQuery, so there is no double-load to
    worry about; if one ever does, move this line there and delete it here rather than having both.

    Self-hosted under wwwroot/lib — the CSP allows script-src 'self' only, so a CDN reference would
    be blocked outright.
*@
<script src="~/lib/jquery/dist/jquery.min.js"></script>
<script src="~/lib/jquery-validation/dist/jquery.validate.min.js"></script>
<script src="~/lib/jquery-validation-unobtrusive/dist/jquery.validate.unobtrusive.min.js"></script>
